.TH GENESIS-MATH 7 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-math \- the parietal mathematics faculties of the Genesis mind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBparietal_lobe.math.number_sense\fR    approximate magnitude (ANS)
\fBparietal_lobe.math.arithmetic\fR      exact arithmetic expressions
\fBparietal_lobe.math.statistics\fR      descriptive and sampling statistics
\fBparietal_lobe.math.symbolic\fR        algebra, calculus, equations, matrices
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The parietal lobe contains several distinct mathematical faculties.
They should not be conflated: approximate magnitude, exact arithmetic,
descriptive statistics, and symbolic mathematics have different
representations and verification limits.
.SS Number sense
.B number_sense.py
implements approximate-number operations: magnitude estimation,
comparison, subitizing, Weber--Fechner scaling, and plausibility
checks. These are estimates and magnitude intuitions, not exact
arithmetic results.
.SS Exact arithmetic
.B arithmetic.py
is a recursive-descent expression evaluator over digits, symbols,
and number/operator words (for example
.IR "7 + 5"
or
.IR "nine times eight" ).
It does not use Python
.BR eval() ;
the expression is parsed and evaluated through explicit operations.
.SS Descriptive statistics
.B statistics.py
implements central tendency, dispersion, distribution shape, and
sampling summaries. It includes the following measures:
.PP
.B Central tendency:
arithmetic, geometric, harmonic, power, quadratic, cubic,
contraharmonic, Heronian, Heinz, Lehmer, median, mode, midrange,
and trimmed means. The Heronian, Heinz, and Lehmer means operate on
two values; they are individual functions, not members of the
.B mean()
dispatcher.
.PP
.B Dispersion:
population or sample variance and standard deviation (sample mode
uses Bessel's correction), mean absolute deviation, median absolute
deviation, percentiles, percentile ranges, interquartile range,
coefficient of variation, and data range.
.PP
.B Shape and sampling:
raw and central moments, skewness, kurtosis (raw or excess), standard
error, and
.B sampling_means()
which draws repeated samples with replacement to inspect the
empirical sampling distribution of the mean. This is a simulation
of sampling behavior, not a proof of the central limit theorem.
.PP
The
.B mean()
dispatcher accepts exactly these
.B MEAN_KINDS:
.IR arithmetic ,
.IR geometric ,
.IR harmonic ,
.IR quadratic ,
.IR cubic ,
.IR contraharmonic ,
.IR power ,
.IR median ,
.IR mode ,
and
.IR midrange .
It does not dispatch to every standalone mean function. The
.B summarize()
facade returns a
.B StatSummary
whose variance and standard deviation are population measures.
.SS Symbolic mathematics
.B symbolic.py
provides a separate symbolic layer backed by SymPy. It is loaded
lazily; when SymPy is not installed, operations that require it
return an unavailable result rather than silently substituting
numeric approximations.
.PP
Supported expression operations include simplification, expansion,
factoring, cancellation, partial fractions, combining rational
expressions, trigonometric simplification, differentiation,
integration (indefinite or definite), equation solving, limits,
series expansion, and 20-digit numerical evaluation. Matrix
operations include determinant, eigenvalues, trace, inverse, and
characteristic polynomial.
.PP
The equality and inequality oracle can return
.IR verified ,
.IR refuted ,
or
.IR undecided .
A bounded equality check that passes every tested integer remains
.IR undecided ;
finite testing is not promoted to a proof. This module is a symbolic
computer-algebra faculty, not a general theorem prover or a
complete proof assistant.
.SH ENTRY POINTS
.TP
.B ParietalMath
The facade used by the rest of the mind. It classifies mathematical
and statistical questions, evaluates arithmetic, dispatches named
means through
.BR MEAN_KINDS ,
and returns statistical summaries.
.TP
.B parietal_lobe.math.statistics
The individual statistical functions when a specific measure is
needed.
.TP
.B parietal_lobe.math.symbolic
The symbolic operations and equality/inequality verdicts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I python/parietal_lobe/math/
The mathematical faculty source.
.TP
.I python/tests/test_statistics.py
Tests for statistical measures and sampling behavior.
.TP
.I python/tests/test_symbolic.py
Tests for symbolic operations and verification verdicts.
.SH LIMITATIONS
These are implemented mathematical faculties, not evidence that
every conversation automatically invokes every operation. The
presence of a callable function does not establish autonomous
mathematical competence across arbitrary problem classes. Symbolic
operations require SymPy; approximate-number results are estimates;
and bounded checks remain evidence rather than general proofs.
